<p>These files contain a ready-to-use Photon database. Download and unpack the file.
Then start Photon from the directory where you have unpacked the tarball.</p>

<p>The database dump only has support for the languages English, German, French
and local language. There is also no support for structured search or full
geometries. If you need more languages or any of the advanced features, use
the JSON data dump.</p>

<p>Please make sure to download the dump that fits with the major release number
of your Photon package. For <b>version 0.7</b>, extracts for both
ElasticSearch 5.6 and OpenSearch are provided. Choose what fits to the
jar file you downloaded.</p>

<p><b>master</b> versions are built with the latest Photon version from GitHub.
They are only guaranteed to work with the version they have been built with, so
use with care.</p>


<h3>Json data dump (jsonl.zst)</h3>

<table>
<thead><tr><th>Photon version</th><th>Json data dump</th><th>Size</th><th>Last update</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
  <td>0.7.x - 1.x</td>
  
  
  <td><a href="https://download1.graphhopper.com/public/photon-dump-planet-1.0-latest.jsonl.zst">photon-dump-planet-1.0-latest.jsonl.zst</a></td>
  <td>27.1 GB</td>
  <td>2026-11-16 06:33:06</td>
  
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>master</td>
  
  
  <td><a href="https://download1.graphhopper.com/public/photon-dump-planet-master-latest.jsonl.zst">photon-dump-planet-master-latest.jsonl.zst</a></td>
  <td>27.1 GB</td>
  <td>2026-11-12 05:23:27</td>
  
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>


<p>This file contains a data dump, which can be used to build your own custom
Photon database. Download the file, then run an import like this:</p>

<p><code>zstd --stdout -d photon-dump-*.jsonl.zst | java -jar photon.jar import -import-file -</code></p>

Json data dumps are guaranteed to work with the Photons versions given.

For more information on data dumps, see the
<a href="https://github.com/komoot/photon/blob/master/docs/usage.md#importing-from-a-dump-file">documentation</a>.



